This project builds on and credits two upstream projects:

1. BMAD-METHOD
   https://github.com/bmad-code-org/BMAD-METHOD
   Copyright (c) BMAD
   Licensed under the MIT License.

   adk-bmad does not reimplement BMAD-METHOD's agent instructions. Instead,
   `src/adk_bmad/skills.py` loads the real upstream "skill" files (SKILL.md,
   steps/*.md, checklist.md, template.md) at runtime — either from a BMAD-METHOD
   project you point it at, or from the vendored fallback copy under
   `src/adk_bmad/vendor/bmad-skills/`, kept in sync via `scripts/sync_bmad_skills.py`.
   See `src/adk_bmad/vendor/bmad-skills/MANIFEST.json` for exactly which upstream
   version is vendored, and `docs/bmad-compatibility.md` for the schema this
   project depends on (sprint-status.yaml, story file format, etc.).

   adk-bmad's own workflow orchestration (the ADK agent graph, tools, callbacks,
   and the parallel adversarial-review gate) is original work — only the BMAD
   domain instructions are sourced from upstream.

2. Google Agent Development Kit (ADK)
   https://github.com/google/adk-python
   Copyright (c) Google LLC
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   adk-bmad is built on the `google-adk` Python package and depends on it at
   runtime; it is not affiliated with or endorsed by Google.

================================================================================

adk-bmad is a sibling project to `archon-bmad` (https://github.com/iameirikr/archon-bmad,
same author), which ports the same BMAD implementation loop onto the Archon
workflow engine. The two are independent implementations of the same idea on
different runtimes.
